        <div class="space-y-4 text-xs md:text-sm text-slate-gray mb-8 leading-relaxed font-light">
          <p>
            <strong class="text-deep-charcoal font-semibold">Challenge:</strong> A growing multi-team organization managed project schedules, headcount, and client assignments across isolated spreadsheets. Updates had to be chased down manually each week, data frequently fell out of sync, and department heads lacked clear visibility into who was available for upcoming work.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-deep-charcoal font-semibold">What We Built:</strong> A centralized capacity and allocation system built natively inside Google Workspace using Google Apps Script. It tied team rosters directly into weekly allocation sheets, automated rollups across departments, enforced view permissions by role, and provided managers with an up-to-date availability dashboard.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-deep-charcoal font-semibold">Outcome:</strong> Deployed across 17 teams and 37 staff members. The client estimated that reducing back-and-forth scheduling messages and manual spreadsheet maintenance saved roughly 16 hours per person each month, totaling about 590 hours saved across the company monthly.
          </p>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-gray/70 italic border-t border-outline-variant/20 pt-3 mt-4">
            * Note: Delivered via our extended network on a large enterprise engagement. Hours saved are client internal estimates.
          </p>
